Central contention

The word imagination currently compresses several different capacities:

generating sensory-like imagery;
entertaining a proposition without believing it;
reconstructing the past;
simulating possible futures;
trying another person’s perspective;
creating symbols, stories, models, and actions;
encountering apparently autonomous inner figures;
allegedly perceiving realities unavailable to ordinary sensation.

