provided the simulation is faithful.

13. Four epistemic failure modes
Model inheritance

Imagination reproduces hidden assumptions in the model.

Availability bias

What is easy to imagine can feel more likely than it is.

Emotional amplification

An affectively powerful scene can be mistaken for evidence.

Source confusion

Generated content can be misattributed to perception, memory, revelation, or another agent.

Therefore:

phenomenological autonomy

=external ontological independence.
