An image can surprise the ego without having originated outside the organism.

This becomes decisive for Jung and Steiner.

VIII. Jung: imagination as dialogue with autonomous psyche
14. What Jung means by active imagination

Jung’s active imagination is not ordinary deliberate visualization.

It begins with spontaneous material such as:

