27. The critical epistemic problem

Steiner’s system claims that trained inner experience can become perception of supersensible realities.

Science can confirm that training alters:

attention;
imagery vividness;
metacognition;
sensory precision;
absorption;
source monitoring;
bodily awareness.

It cannot confirm from the experience alone that its content originates in an independently existing spiritual realm.

The inferential step is:

